WEBVTT

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.540
The private school, Kamizono Academy.  Established in '56.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.410
If you combine the elementary, middle, and high schools,

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.020
it has a student population of more than 3,000.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.960
"To inspire talent in all directions, no matter what the field!" is the school's motto.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.670
Tatsuki-chan!

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.030
And this is the building in which these girls study.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.030
Good morning!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.540
Tatsuki-chan!  I said, "Good morning!"

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.050
A bit over-familiar, aren't we?

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.950
Just call me friendly.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.590
It has not been that many days since we all met each other.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.870
But didn't we bond while receiving all that educational "guidance?"

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.890
I have no wish to hang out with someone who even skipped out on the entrance ceremony.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.760
Will you refrain from speaking to me?

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:45.290
So anyway, it seems like if you want to join a club you have to decide by today.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.980
She ignored me.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.900
But it's not like you absolutely have to join a club, right?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:59.770
Well, it's not compulsory, but I just thought it'd be like true friendship if the four of us joined the same club!

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:00.820
No it would not.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.990
The four of us already "Best Friends Forever!"

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:30.890
Will you please stop this childish coercion tactics?

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.480
The four of us, BFF?

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.150
Not me.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.110
Kage's Gang-of-Four!

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.820
Stop counting me with the rest of you.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.220
The Kage Quad-Squad!

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.780
The Four Kage Kings!

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:57.170
Kage Girl's Group...

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.440
Kagekage 4!

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.180
Wait, what are you thinking?!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.110
Uh, right.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.890
Do not fall into her trap.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.260
Like this, here...

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.100
Quit it, I said!

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.790
Oh, Touma!  Good morning!

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.140
Ayu, did you see that?  Hear that?

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.590
That Touma chick just clicked her tongue at me!

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.060
And who was that?

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.020
She sits in the seat next to Torako-san.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.330
Touma, you jerk!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.410
What is <i>with</i> her?

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.130
So, what club should we join?

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.010
I do not have any intention of participating in-

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.920
They said they'd be handing out a list, right?

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.880
She ignored me again.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.770
Hey, class is about to start.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:46.550
Good morning!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.630
Hurry up and get to class.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.800
Is that the list of clubs?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.520
I'm going to pass them out, so get to class.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.300
Just give one to me now!

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.490
Take your seat first!

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:57.060
Tightwad!

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.100
I am not a tightwad!

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.150
Stubborn jerk!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.620
I am not stubborn!!

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.720
Useless bum!

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.830
Kageyama... teacher's office, after school...

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:14.370
So, so... have you decided what club to join?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.960
Club?

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.960
Oh yeah!  That's right!

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.840
I appreciate the sentiment, however I have no intention of joining any club activities.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.910
And besides, did I not request that you refrain from speaking to me so often?

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:33.020
And have I not been saying that for the two weeks since school started?

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.390
And more than five times just today?

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.340
So, what club should we do?

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.460
A sports club?  A humanities club?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.870
And this is <i>also</i> the fifth time you've <i>ignored</i> me today!

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.660
Wow, I don't know where to start!

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.150
Is that the list?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:56.040
From appreciation clubs to societies, when you include them all there's more than 100 of them!

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:01.050
Baseball, soccer, tennis obviously, but there's even curling and lacrosse!

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.960
Whoa, they even have kabaddi!

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.960
NOTE:  Really said "kava tea."

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:08.110
Flower arrangement club, tea ceremony club, magic society, robot society...

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:14.450
Black magic society, white magic society, red magic and blue magic?

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:19.170
The society for the appreciation of fantasy literature, society for the study of modern literature...

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.850
There are a lot of them, aren't there?

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:25.150
There sure are!  It's an all-you-can choose buffet!

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:35.330
Black Magic Society!  <i>Curse You
Funny Story Society</i>

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:35.330
Literary Club

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:29.010
I guess it really is better to join some sort of club.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.380
Let's do it!

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.930
Everything seems really fun.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:36.850
Yeah!  This is definitely the true taste of school life!

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:40.040
But, I'm not very good at sports...

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.770
If I must repeat myself, I have no intention of participating in-

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.770
What would you like?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.060
The sixth time...

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.560
The sixth time she's ignored me...

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.800
Um, yeah, let's see...

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:54.850
What, what?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:58.890
Literary Club

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.220
How about the literary club?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.310
How about you, Suzu?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.690
She ignored me, too.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.880
Cafe...

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.780
Cafeteria.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.120
What was that?

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:23.540
White Magic Society
<i>Curaga...</i>

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:23.540
Red Magic Society
<i>Firaga Stona</i>

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:23.540
Summon Magic Society
<i>Escape...</i>

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.850
The cafeteria isn't a club, y'know.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:23.540
Black Magic Society
<i>Meteor</i>

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:21.420
You can go to it everyday anyway.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.540
Really?  I see.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.750
What do you want to do?

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.470
Eh?  I guess I want to do that.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.440
That?

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.630
You know, <i>that</i>.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.090
What?

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.760
The baseball club!

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.310
Bring it on!

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.900
Let's do this!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:48.190
Now look here, what exactly do you intend to do with just the four of us?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.930
You call this a club activity?

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:53.580
Um... I'm not really any good at baseball...

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:57.000
I can't help it!  Those guys said girls couldn't play.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.060
Although they let us borrow the equipment.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:03.200
Sorry for borrowing your equipment!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.000
No prob.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:14.510
Fine!  Then we'll establish our own women's baseball club!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.050
Our goal:  the Koushien!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.160
Whoa!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.960
"Whoa?"

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.170
I at least want to change clothes...

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.690
Okay, let's decide what positions we'll play.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.610
Note:  Ichiro Suzuki

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.610
I'll be Ichizou!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.230
No, that is not a position.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.030
Note:  Kazuhiro Kiyohara

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.030
Suzu, you're Kiyohata.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.000
That is also wrong!

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:34.860
Note:  Hideki Matsui

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:34.860
Ayu, you're Machui!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:35.960
You are so annoying!

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:38.510
And anyway, all of us are batters!

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:41.160
With only 3 people, there are not any positions anyway!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:47.610
All right then, how about if you hit it back you get one point, and if I get it past you I get one point.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.830
Now look here...

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:52.340
It's hardly even baseball anymore, is it?

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.630
This is ridiculous.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:59.330
I am leaving.

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:02.320
Hey, you!  Are you running away?

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.080
Running away, you say?

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.400
Are you running away?

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.830
Running away?  I am-

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.690
Are you running away?

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.790
You <i>are</i> running away.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:19.320
Bring it on!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.780
W-Wait, Tatsuki-san...

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:24.620
I see you've finally got the spirit.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.230
Ayu, be the umpire!

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:34.030
Okay!  But I got a glove and everything...

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.220
You won't be able to hit this so easily!

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:40.010
Because me and Suzu are the ultimate-

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.890
Um... What was that again?

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.900
The ultimate... Um...

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:55.000
Oh, right.  Because we're the ultimate engineers!

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.150
Huh?  Engineers?

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.380
Wait, did you mean "battery?"

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:02.240
Right, that!  Battery, battery!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:03.030
Balk.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:07.000
Here we go!  The ultimate battery!

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.140
Sorry...

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.910
That hurt!  That hurt!  That hurt!

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.870
I said I was sorry, sheesh!

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.000
Sign

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.640
Let's try the next one!

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:07.180
When it comes to girl's sports clubs, it's got to be tennis.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.560
If you want to say it in Japanese, it's "teikyuu."  Take you!

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:18.060
Well, at least this we can do with only four people.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:19.540
No kidding!

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:22.200
And it seems they let us borrow some clothes.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.620
Yeah!  Everyone looks great!

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.270
Suzume-san?

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.780
They said we could use this court all we wanted.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:32.570
Even though we don't necessarily intend to join the tennis club?

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:34.890
Just tryin' it out, tryin' it out.

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:36.250
A try out...

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.310
They seem to be watching us, though...

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:39.910
Don't worry 'bout it!

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.330
We're sorry!

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.760
Okay!  This is the founding of the the Kamizono Academy Tennis Club #2!

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.900
Our goal:  Wimbledon!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.100
Whoa!

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.970
Tennis Club #2?

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.280
Huh...

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:06.120
Since there are four of us, let's play a doubles match!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.300
We'll split up with me and Suzu are one pair,

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:12.000
and over there, Tatsuki-chan and Ayu.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.560
Says you.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.620
Let's have a good game.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.090
Note:  Maria Sharapova

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.090
As for positions, I'm Sharapoka!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.370
And now she has started this again...

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:22.670
Note:  Martina Hingis

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:22.670
Suzu, you're Hingiso.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.890
Note: Ochoufujin (Madame Butterfly) - Reika from "Ace wo Nerae"

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.890
And Tatsuki-chan, you're Otatasu Fujin!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.240
Is that not a manga character?

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.140
Tatsuki-san?

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:32.140
Note:  "Ace wo Nerae" art style

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.460
As you wish.

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:32.610
This will not be like what happened before.

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.560
That's good!  That's the spirit!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.500
Here we go, Ayumi!

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.010
Yes, Coach!

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:39.900
That is not exactly right, but...

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:41.980
Fine, whatever.

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.460
I'll be taking first serve!

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:46.880
Do as you please.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:49.200
We aren't going to spin a racket?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.400
Huh?  Do what with the racket?  Spin it?

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:53.580
Get on with it!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.900
I'll let you have one of my "tiger smashes!"

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.210
What an inane name.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:00.920
Bring it on!

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:08.340
Here it comes!

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.180
Right!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.630
Fault.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:19.740
Okay, that was good for the first time.  This time for real!

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:21.510
Great Tiger Smash!

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:22.750
Great?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:23.700
That's right.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:24.440
Hurry up!

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:29.660
This time it's really coming!

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.050
Right!

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.330
Double fault.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.670
Sorry...

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.550
To~ra~ko~

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:53.250
You did that on purpose!  You did that on purpose!

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:57.000
It wasn't on purpose!

00:13:57.510 --> 00:14:00.310
It was so definitely on purpose!

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.310
Let's try the next one!

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:10.160
Go!  Go!  Kamizono!  Go!  Go!  Kamizono!  Yay!

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.440
I cannot take much more.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:15.640
They did give is numbered jerseys, though.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:20.080
Note:  The number 4 is usually avoided on a jersey because it's pronounced the same as "death" (shi).

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.040
Why?

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:21.380
And they not only let us borrow these jerseys, but even an entire court once again.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.730
Everyone's just really nice.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.760
We're sorry!

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:30.800
I wonder if Torako-san is really popular?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.160
I doubt that.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:37.310
Well, why not?  If we do good, then they'll get four new club members.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.440
I have never said that I would join a club.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:43.230
I never did, either...

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:46.580
Okay!  This is the founding of the "New" Girls Basketball club!

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.650
Our goal:  Madison Square Garden!

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.420
Whoa!

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:51.420
And another slogan...

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.320
So we're continuing this pattern?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.450
I'm Magic Something!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.720
And Suzu is Michael Something.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.460
The Dream Team.

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.220
And who are you two going to be?

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:07.420
I think the teams have already been decided...

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.420
Are there any other famous basketball players?

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:10.890
You're playing along?

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.130
Note:  From "Slam Dunk"

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.130
Taduki-chan, you're Gori.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.570
Huh?  Gori?  Who?

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.260
Oh, I don't know.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.020
Note:  From "Dash Kappei"

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.020
Ayu, you're Kappei!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.400
Huh?  Who?

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:21.850
Dash!

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.730
First we'll have a free throw competition.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.370
Don't throw it at the same time!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:41.160
Well, then you should have said so in the first place.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:43.670
Fine.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.920
But, that's not how this game works!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:57.620
It seems you still have not realized.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.110
Realized what?

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:01.280
Try another shot.

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.550
And the point is...

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:10.220
It's the same thing three times in a row!

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:13.700
Do you understand the meaning of these precise moves?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.190
What?

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:17.370
This time it is my turn.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.080
Please, let's just move on...

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.610
It doesn't look like we're going to decide anything with free throws.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:36.670
Are not you the one who keeps doing all these inane things?

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:39.440
But you were the one who started it here!

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:42.050
What?  Are you saying that this time it is my fault?

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:44.140
Whatever!  It's a jump ball!  Hurry up and toss it!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:48.480
And she ignores me for the infuriatingly umpteenth time...

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.170
Ayu!

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.020
R-Right!

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:53.140
Don't agree!  You can't throw the ball!

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:55.420
There's no jump balls when it's 2-on-2!

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:56.570
Who would receive it?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:57.200
Okay then, Suzu!

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.750
W-Wait!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.620
Attack!

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:14.170
Sorry...

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:19.170
Torako!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.350
Let's try the next one!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.790
Next!

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:28.980
Tea Ceremony

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.400
They're neither refined, nor elegant...

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.240
In fact, it's more like a battle...

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.960
Next!

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:50.000
Look here, you guys!  Please, stop!

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:56.130
Tiger Trap

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.130
Next!

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:04.100
We can't have a proper contest in these humanities clubs.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.420
That is true.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:09.390
Um, we were searching for a club, weren't we?

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:10.770
Next!

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:15.200
They said that the soccer club's practice was over for today.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.740
And told us to use it all we wanted.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.740
We're really sorry!

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.950
Our goal:  The World Cup!

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.590
You're going to do it, aren't you?

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:25.550
Whoa!

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:29.600
Who cares about the World Cup?

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.210
All I want to do is pay you back for what you have done.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.750
Sounds good!  The fated tournament!

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.720
It only started today, though...

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.170
That's not true.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:44.430
This is my chance to break away from this group she arbitrarily formed since the first day of school.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.280
But, that's just...

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.600
You have not been directly damaged, so you would not understand.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.030
Note: Ronaldinho

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.030
Okay, then I'm Ronaldino!

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.650
Note:  Hidetoshi Nakata

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.650
And I'm Nakato!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.700
Note:  Ivica Osim

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.700
Huh?  Be Oshimo!

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.240
But he is a manager!

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.330
Note:  Oliver Kahn

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.330
Suzu, you're Oliver-kun, okay?

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:09.450
How about Kaka?

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.670
Note:  Yoshikatsu Kawaguchi

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.670
Ayu, you're Kawaguche.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.200
So then, it is okay for me to be Nakata, right?

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.150
The match will be PK, Sudden Death!

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.420
Fine with me.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:21.970
At least it seems like you do not have anything to injure me with in this setup.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.800
Wait, make sure to tie the lace properly on your spike shoes.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:28.720
You would not have...

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.270
...been thinking of something like that?

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.470
Of course not.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:36.640
Anyway, you go first.

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:38.210
Don't just decide that yourself!

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:42.140
When it comes to penalty kicks, if the person who goes first misses, it puts them at quite a disadvantage.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.820
All you can see if the image of you missing, and you end up losing.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.410
But if you make it, you put serious pressure on your opponent.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:50.250
Pressure doesn't mean anything to me.

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:52.250
Perhaps so.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.700
Either way is fine with me.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:56.380
If you want to go second, have Ayu stand in the goal.

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.820
Fine, I will go first.

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:02.170
I'm sorry...

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.630
I'm counting on you, Suzu!

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.110
If you miss, it's obvious who'll win between me and Ayu.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:11.180
Please don't miss!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:13.480
Suzu's a tough cookie, you know.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:15.440
We will see about that.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.850
She does not seem at her best condition.

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:28.530
Suzu, once this is over we'll go to the cafeteria!

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.170
Cafeteria?!

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:31.300
Extra-large kitsune udon!

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:32.480
You'll treat me?

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:33.290
My treat!

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.970
Can I have a tendon (tempura w/rice), too?

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:36.780
Uh... fine!

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.950
The cafeteria is already closed...

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:42.350
Here I come!

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.910
Oh no, I slipped!

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.030
Sorry!

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.150
But...

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:13.310
You seriously think I would believe that was a <i>slip</i>?!

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:18.210
Umpire! Umpire! Injury time-out! Injury time-out!

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.840
Suzume-san?

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:28.160
I have had enough! Taste the ultimate peak of my rage!

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:38.810
Hey, everyone! Let's do the takkyu club today!  Takkyu!

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.700
Or, as they say in English, ping-pong!

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:44.740
Huh, where's Ta-chan.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.370
She went home.

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:22.480
Um, what's up next week on Hyakko?

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:24.250
The tiger at the front gates, and the tiger at the school gates.

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:25.460
There's even something called a "paper tiger."

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:26.530
Two of them are standing there.

00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:28.090
The school gates are at the entrance to the school, right?

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:29.540
Either one of them is a tiger, so we're in big trouble.

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:31.170
But the one at the rear gate is actually a cat, right?

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:32.470
And there's nothing scary about a paper tiger!

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:34.280
Look forward to next time too!
